    "excerpt": "In recent years, artificial intelligence (AI) has become a true game changer in software development. AI is automating many tasks such as writing code, fixing bugs, testing and…",
    "readingTime": 2,
    "html": "<p>In recent years, artificial intelligence (AI) has become a true game changer in software development. AI is automating many tasks such as writing code, fixing bugs, testing and documentation, multiplying developer productivity several times over.</p>\n<p>In this article, we introduce the 5 AI tools most widely used by developers around the world, along with their features and real-world usage examples.</p>\n<h2 id=\"1-github-copilot--your-ai-pair-programmer\">1. GitHub Copilot – Your AI Pair Programmer</h2>\n<p>GitHub Copilot is an AI assistant built on OpenAI's GPT models that offers real-time suggestions as you write code.</p>\n<p><strong>Key advantages</strong>:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Automatically writes lines of code, functions and even complete classes</li>\n<li>Supports many languages, including Python, JavaScript, Java, C++ and Go</li>\n<li>Integrates directly with IDEs such as VS Code, JetBrains and Neovim</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Why do developers use it so much?</strong></p>\n<p>GitHub Copilot noticeably speeds up coding and reduces repetitive work. That is why many developers call it an \"AI pair programmer\".</p>\n<h2 id=\"2-chatgpt--a-universal-assistant-for-code-and-logic\">2. ChatGPT – A Universal Assistant for Code and Logic</h2>\n<p>ChatGPT is not just for writing text; it is a versatile AI tool for developers.</p>\n<p><strong>Common use cases:</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Explaining and fixing bugs</li>\n<li>Explaining algorithms and data structures</li>\n<li>Quickly learning new technologies and frameworks</li>\n<li>Generating example code for APIs and functions</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Advantages:</strong></p>\n<p>Because ChatGPT can think about the big picture and explain logic outside the IDE, it is equally useful to junior and senior developers.</p>\n<h2 id=\"3-cursor-ai--a-code-editor-with-built-in-ai\">3. Cursor AI – A Code Editor with Built-in AI</h2>\n<p>Cursor is a next-generation code editor with AI built into its core.</p>\n<p><strong>Features:</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Able to work with large codebases</li>\n<li>Analyzes multiple files at once and suggests refactors</li>\n<li>Lets you run commands such as \"Explain this code\" and \"Fix this bug\" directly from within your code</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Who is it for?</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Developers who work on large projects</li>\n<li>Developers who maintain legacy code</li>\n<li>Developers who want AI at the center of their IDE</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"4-tabnine--fast-secure-code-autocomplete\">4. Tabnine – Fast, Secure Code Autocomplete</h2>\n<p>Tabnine is an AI-powered code autocomplete tool and another popular alternative to Copilot.</p>\n<p><strong>Advantages:</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Supports many IDEs and programming languages</li>\n<li>Well suited to enterprise-level use</li>\n<li>Can run locally (offline) in some configurations</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Why use it?</strong></p>\n<p>Tabnine is a better fit for teams that prioritize code security and speed.</p>\n<h2 id=\"5-qodo-codiumai--ai-code-checker-and-code-review\">5. Qodo (CodiumAI) – AI Code Checker and Code Review</h2>\n<p>Qodo (formerly CodiumAI) is an AI tool focused on code quality, testing and review.</p>\n<p><strong>What can it do?</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Automatically generates unit tests</li>\n<li>Performs code reviews and suggests improvements</li>\n<li>Works in tandem with CI/CD pipelines</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Benefits:</strong></p>\n<p>This tool keeps a team's code quality consistent and reduces the time spent on manual review.</p>"
